<title>FRANCE: EU may end 96/97 wheat exports before end April.</title>
<headline>EU may end 96/97 wheat exports before end April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union may wrap up soft wheat exports for the 1996/97 campaign before the traditional end-April deadline, having already exported substantial volumes, an EU Commission official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not very far from the end of the campaign. It may be over before end-April,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Since the start of the 1996/97 (July/June) season, the European Union has exported 8.1 million tonnes of soft wheat grain, the official said.</p>
<p>This compares with exports of a little over five million tonnes during the same period for 1995/96 when stocks were tight and wheat prices high.</p>
</text>
